# Accessibility — WCAG 2.1 AA

## Perceivable

- Images need meaningful `alt` (decorative → `alt=""` + `aria-hidden`).
- Maintain WCAG contrast ratios — use `--color-primary` / `--color-secondary` tokens which have been verified.
- Support 200% zoom and 320px width without horizontal scroll.
- Don't rely on color alone.
- Use Tailwind's `leading-normal` or `leading-relaxed` (maps to 1.5–1.625) for body text.

## Operable

- All controls must be keyboard accessible.
- Add a skip link to `#content` — use the `skip-link` `@utility` from `style.css`.
- Never remove focus outlines — use Tailwind's `focus:outline-none` only when paired with a visible `focus:ring-*` alternative.
- Use `focus-visible:` variants over `focus:` where possible to avoid focus rings on mouse clicks.
- Links should be descriptive.

## Understandable

- Use `language_attributes()`.
- One `<h1>` per page; blocks start with `<h2>`.
- Every form field needs a label — use `class="sr-only"` for visually hidden labels (Tailwind utility).
- Show accessible error messages.

## Robust

- Use semantic landmarks (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `footer`).
- Add required ARIA for accordions, tabs, modals, alerts, and toggles.
- Use `aria-live` for dynamic content.

## Tailwind Accessibility Utilities

| Need | Tailwind class |
|---|---|
| Screen reader only text | `sr-only` |
| Reveal on focus | `focus:not-sr-only` |
| Skip link (full pattern) | `skip-link` `@utility` |
| Focus ring | `focus:ring-2 focus:ring-primary focus:ring-offset-2` |
| Hide from AT | `aria-hidden="true"` (attribute, not a class) |

## Never

- `outline: none` without a visible alternative
- `tabindex > 0`
- Interactive `<div>`/`<span>` without keyboard support
- Placeholder as a label
- Color-only indicators

**Always:** Include `sr-only` where needed and perform keyboard + screen reader testing before delivery.
